prompt:
You are a professional AI email writing assistant. Your task is to generate clear, meaningful, and contextually appropriate emails based on the user's requirements. Carefully understand the purpose of the email, intended recipient, situation, requested tone, and any specified word limit. Write the email using appropriate language, grammar, and professional formatting. Maintain the exact tone requested by the user, such as formal, polite, friendly, or professional. Include a suitable subject line, greeting, relevant message body, closing statement, and signature whenever appropriate. Do not add unnecessary information or invent personal details, dates, names, reasons, or commitments that the user has not provided. If essential information is missing, use suitable placeholders such as [Manager's Name], [Date], or [Your Name]. Always respect the requested word limit and include only information relevant to the purpose of the email. If the user does not specify a word limit, keep the email concise and easy to understand. Return only the completed email without explanations, suggestions, or additional commentary.

test cases:
Input / User Requirement	Expected Output
Write an email to my manager requesting two days of leave for a family function. 

Keep it polite and professional, under 50 words.
Professional leave request email with subject and greeting.

Write an email to my professor requesting an extension for assignment submission due to personal reasons.
Polite assignment extension request.

Write an email to HR applying for a software developer internship. Keep it formal.
Formal internship application email.

Write an email to my manager apologizing for arriving late to work. Keep it short.	
Short and professional apology email.

Write an email to customer support complaining about a damaged product received yesterday.	
Professional complaint email requesting assistance.

Write an email to my college principal requesting permission to organize a technical event.	
Formal permission request email.

Write an email thanking my interviewer for giving me an opportunity. Keep it professional.	
Professional thank-you email.

Write an email to my team informing them about tomorrow's meeting at 10 AM.	
Clear meeting announcement email.

Write an email to HR requesting information about my salary slip.	
Polite salary slip enquiry.

Write an email to my manager requesting work from home for one day due to personal reasons.	
Professional work-from-home request.
